
Logical Operators in MongoDb:

$and: 
---------- >
..> Returns docyuments where both queries match.
Syntax:  { $and : [condition1,condition2] }

db.collections_name.find( {filed1:"Value });

{"age": { $lt:20 }} + {"city:"Delhi" }
{"age" : {$gt:20 }} + {"age" :{$lt:30 }}

ex: db.MySkills.find({
  $and:[ { "age":{$gt:40}}]
})l

$or
-------- >
Returns documents where either query matches.

Syntax: { $or : [condition1,cpnditions2 ] }

Ex:db.MySkills.find({
  $or:[ { "age":{$gt:40}},{"name":{$eq:"sai"}}]
})

$nor:
----------- >
Returns documents where both queries fail to match.

Syntax : { $nor : [conditions1, conditions2 ] }

Ex:db.MySkills.find({
  $nor:[ { "age":{$gt:40}},{"name":{$eq:"sai"}}]
})

$not :
--------- .
Returns documents where the query does not match.

Syntax: { $not : [ condition ] }
 
Ex:
db.MySkills.find(
   { "age":{$not:{$gt:80}}}
)

